      Above 1000 keV                                              1637 1451
        mt=1,2,4,51-55,91,102                                     1637 1451
           Total, elastic, inelastic and capture                  1637 1451
         calculated with casthy code /2/, considering the         1637 1451
         competition with the threshold reaction channels.        1637 1451
           Optical potential parameters of C.Y.Fu/3/ are adjusted 1637 1451
         to reproduce the following experimental data:            1637 1451
             mt=1  total -                                        1637 1451
             mt=2  elastic cross sections of s-32                 1637 1451
             mt=4  inelastic -                                    1637 1451
         The spherical optical potential parameters:              1637 1451
             V = 38.0      Vso= 5.37  (MeV)                       1637 1451
             Ws= 9.13      Wv = 0.0   (MeV)                       1637 1451
             r =rso= 1.26  rs = 1.39  (fm)                        1637 1451
             a =aso= 0.76  b  = 0.40  (fm)                        1637 1451
           mt=102 capture data are normalized to 0.15 mb at 1 MeV 1637 1451
         based on s-32 capture cross section.                     1637 1451
           The discrete level scheme taken from ref./4/:          1637 1451
             no.     energy (MeV)     spin-parity                 1637 1451
           (g.s.)      0.0              0   +                     1637 1451
              1        3.291            2   +                     1637 1451
              2        3.346            0   +                     1637 1451
              3        4.192            3   -                     1637 1451
              4        4.523            1   +                     1637 1451
              5        4.575            2   +                     1637 1451
         Continuum levels assumed above 5.0 MeV. The level        1637 1451
         density parameters of Asano et al./5/ are used.          1637 1451
